WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:26.657 --> 00:00:29.560
We're three kilometers
off the coast, Vertigo.


00:00:30.928 --> 00:00:32.564
Keep it steady, Manta.


00:00:34.032 --> 00:00:35.800
I'll go rouse the rabble.


00:00:38.336 --> 00:00:39.805
Time to move.


00:00:40.772 --> 00:00:42.671
I'm good to go.


00:00:42.673 --> 00:00:45.140
Sponge and Julie, not so sure.


00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:47.542
Didn't Waller get you
a room last night?


00:00:47.544 --> 00:00:49.478
Don't be a hater, Floyd.


00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:53.015
Or are you just upset because
Waller didn't put you in charge.


00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:57.018
Yeah, why is that, Deadshot?
You usually run things.


00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:00.289
She asked me if her dress
made her look fat.


00:01:00.291 --> 00:01:02.491
She's gotten cranky
since she lost weight.


00:01:02.493 --> 00:01:05.595
Not our issue.
Is it, Daddy?


00:01:05.597 --> 00:01:10.732
We are just having our second
honeymoon anywhere we can.


00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:13.735
<i>Not on my time, convict.</i>


00:01:13.737 --> 00:01:19.241
<i>The only one who gets
satisfied tonight is me.</i>


00:01:19.243 --> 00:01:24.813
<i>Your target is an underboss in the
Black Mask mob, Tobias Whale,</i>


00:01:24.815 --> 00:01:28.217
<i>who happens to sideline
in stolen intel.</i>


00:01:28.219 --> 00:01:31.553
<i>Tonight, he's delivering a
flash drive full of nastiness.</i>


00:01:31.555 --> 00:01:37.726
<i>Pay-offs to dictators, senators playing
footsies in the restroom, the usual.</i>


00:01:37.728 --> 00:01:40.163
<i>More importantly,
he has leaked info</i>


00:01:40.165 --> 00:01:43.932
<i>implicating our
very own operations.</i>


00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:47.970
<i>Needless to say, Mama would be very
disappointed if you screwed this up.</i>


00:01:47.972 --> 00:01:50.172
<i>So keep your heads
on the mission</i>


00:01:50.174 --> 00:01:52.511
<i>if you want to keep them
on your shoulders.</i>


00:01:53.344 --> 00:01:54.579
<i>Any questions?</i>


00:01:55.213 --> 00:01:56.678
<i>Good.</i>


00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.582
<i>They're all yours, Vertigo.</i>


00:02:00.184 --> 00:02:02.587
<i>I'll be on radio silence
till you're done.</i>


00:02:03.621 --> 00:02:05.090
<i>Waller out.</i>


00:02:06.624 --> 00:02:08.093
You heard the lady.


00:02:39.556 --> 00:02:41.224
Show off.


00:03:00.177 --> 00:03:01.846
All right, goddamn it.


00:04:14.952 --> 00:04:19.087
So I says if the money's good,
who gives a shit, huh?


00:04:21.491 --> 00:04:23.226
Hey. Oh...


00:04:31.569 --> 00:04:33.839
Ah! Oh. Ugh!


00:04:38.875 --> 00:04:40.375
Ah!


00:04:50.854 --> 00:04:52.921
You still got it, baby.


00:04:52.923 --> 00:04:55.160
And it's all yours, Daddy.


00:06:25.048 --> 00:06:27.483
You're that fool, Deadshot.


00:06:27.485 --> 00:06:29.351
Ain't this some shit?


00:06:29.353 --> 00:06:33.022
Did Black Mask find out about
my sidekick and send you?


00:06:35.925 --> 00:06:39.560
I'm gonna mess you up real good.


00:06:39.562 --> 00:06:41.199
It's his turn.


00:07:16.034 --> 00:07:21.072
Expletive deleted and the
free world is saved again.


00:07:28.613 --> 00:07:29.947
Stay down, dog.


00:07:30.914 --> 00:07:32.613
What the heck's going on?


00:07:32.615 --> 00:07:34.385
This wasn't part of the mission.


00:07:35.219 --> 00:07:36.654
Vertigo...


00:07:48.264 --> 00:07:49.498
Why?


00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.836
Aw, honeymoon's over.


00:07:56.639 --> 00:07:58.142
What about him?


00:08:00.911 --> 00:08:03.578
I'd rather not kill him
at the same wound.


00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.681
He'd wonder about that.


00:08:05.683 --> 00:08:09.418
I say we let the train
run him over.


00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.952
You're working together?


00:08:10.954 --> 00:08:13.455
Working, playing...


00:08:13.457 --> 00:08:14.989
We're soulmates.


00:08:14.991 --> 00:08:17.827
Even in prison, things can be


00:08:17.829 --> 00:08:20.029
arranged.


00:08:20.031 --> 00:08:22.296
What about the file?


00:08:22.298 --> 00:08:25.099
We make a copy,
give Waller back the original.


00:08:25.101 --> 00:08:26.601
She'll never know


00:08:26.603 --> 00:08:31.207
and then, when the grieving
widow and I are paroled,


00:08:31.209 --> 00:08:33.344
we'll have a little nest-egg.


00:08:34.377 --> 00:08:35.814
She knows.


00:08:36.281 --> 00:08:37.449
What?


00:08:38.081 --> 00:08:39.183
Waller.


00:08:40.584 --> 00:08:42.150
<i>She's been listening.</i>


00:08:42.152 --> 00:08:45.053
<i>You're lying,
I'm team leader.</i>


00:08:45.055 --> 00:08:47.157
She knew there was
a traitor somewhere.


00:08:52.496 --> 00:08:55.867
Waller? Listen to me, I beg to you.


00:09:10.882 --> 00:09:16.686
Floyd, please, don't let her.


00:09:16.688 --> 00:09:19.020
I know, I know I was a bad girl.


00:09:19.022 --> 00:09:21.756
And it was all Vertigo's idea.


00:09:21.758 --> 00:09:24.760
Please don't let her
kill me, Floyd!


00:09:27.131 --> 00:09:29.067
Don't let her blow my head off.


00:09:34.638 --> 00:09:37.573
She's down, Waller. Turn it off.


00:09:37.575 --> 00:09:39.674
<i>A mercy killing.</i>


00:09:39.676 --> 00:09:41.512
Getting soft on me, Lawton?


00:09:46.751 --> 00:09:49.154
Just saving on the dry cleaning.


00:10:22.552 --> 00:10:24.752
Stop this madness.


00:10:24.754 --> 00:10:26.321
You can't get rid of me.


00:10:26.323 --> 00:10:30.192
I am not some vestigial twin
you can excise like a skin tag.


00:10:30.194 --> 00:10:34.329
Hey, Doc, I'm getting sick
of hearing this guy's crap.


00:10:34.331 --> 00:10:37.000
Ain't you got something
that'll knock him out.


00:10:37.568 --> 00:10:39.137
Anasthetic!


00:10:41.906 --> 00:10:43.541
Where is the anasthetic?


00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:50.212
Well, that's just peachy.


00:10:50.214 --> 00:10:53.882
No anasthetic?
You're all insane!


00:10:53.884 --> 00:10:56.451
Shut your pie hole,
we're gonna do this.


00:10:56.453 --> 00:11:01.259
Just show me again, Doc,
one more time.


00:11:04.561 --> 00:11:05.794
Voila.


00:11:05.796 --> 00:11:09.200
Beautiful.


00:11:10.501 --> 00:11:12.237
No. No. No. No!


00:11:29.887 --> 00:11:31.388
Drill.


00:11:34.324 --> 00:11:38.626
We'll start around the eye.


00:11:44.669 --> 00:11:47.770
Oh, thank God, he was
going to disfigure me.


00:11:47.772 --> 00:11:49.373
That lunatic. That...


00:11:50.541 --> 00:11:52.274
How dare you?


00:11:52.276 --> 00:11:56.381
This is an operating theater
not some abattoir.


00:11:58.114 --> 00:12:00.548
We have a patient
for you, Professor.


00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:03.452
A person in need of
medical attention.


00:12:03.454 --> 00:12:07.291
We're wondering if you could
clear your schedule. Hmm?


00:12:09.392 --> 00:12:14.197
A patient in need is always
my first consideration.


00:12:15.166 --> 00:12:16.566
Good answer.


00:12:55.205 --> 00:12:56.541
Mail call, Lawton.


00:13:19.597 --> 00:13:21.299
Morning, sunshine.


00:13:22.867 --> 00:13:25.502
Get another offer from
Gun Fund Monthly, did you?


00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.601
No, wait a tick.


00:13:27.603 --> 00:13:29.339
It's your little girl, isn't it?


00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:35.044
Aw, did she reject another
letter from dear old dad?


00:13:35.046 --> 00:13:37.880
How old is she now, 13, 14?


00:13:37.882 --> 00:13:42.453
Her uncle bought her any more, eh?
I get bored crazy in that age.


00:13:44.787 --> 00:13:47.822
Tell you what, girls like her
need a daddy.


00:13:47.824 --> 00:13:50.992
How'd you reckon?
Well, get paroled early


00:13:50.994 --> 00:13:53.030
maybe Uncle Digger
can look her up.


00:13:55.165 --> 00:13:58.098
Oh! Christ! Son of a...


00:13:58.100 --> 00:13:59.501
You could've put my eye out.


00:13:59.503 --> 00:14:00.903
Must be gettin' rusty.


00:14:00.905 --> 00:14:03.337
Boomer's government property.


00:14:03.339 --> 00:14:05.075
You break it, you buy it.


00:14:05.908 --> 00:14:07.411
Hiya, cowboy.


00:14:08.645 --> 00:14:10.477
How's Trix?


00:14:10.479 --> 00:14:12.649
Oh, not that crazy broad again.


00:14:13.983 --> 00:14:16.518
My choices have been
dwindling lately.


00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:18.920
I heard about
poor little Julie?


00:14:18.922 --> 00:14:20.654
Beats all my luck, you know.


00:14:20.656 --> 00:14:25.562
But I offered to give her a whole
new makeover with a baseball bat.


00:14:28.098 --> 00:14:29.231
Who else?


00:14:29.233 --> 00:14:30.531
You heard of Killer Frost?


00:14:30.533 --> 00:14:32.568
- The ice queen.
- Yeah.


00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:35.571
Crystal Frost, a tough girl
from a tougher home.


00:14:35.573 --> 00:14:37.972
<i>Her parents were, well...</i>


00:14:37.974 --> 00:14:41.776
<i>Let's just say they could've
used some discipline themselves.</i>


00:14:41.778 --> 00:14:45.047
<i>Then her metahuman powers
kicked in,</i>


00:14:45.049 --> 00:14:48.086
<i>and suddenly, Mom and Dad
were put on ice.</i>


00:14:57.728 --> 00:15:01.730
<i>They never knew how cold
her heart really was.</i>


00:15:01.732 --> 00:15:08.270
<i>They say she couldn't be tamed, but I think
Little Crystal's warmed up to us considerably.</i>


00:15:08.272 --> 00:15:14.409
And then there's Copperhead, AKA
Sameer Park, a meta contortionist


00:15:14.411 --> 00:15:17.045
<i>heavily into extreme
body modification.</i>


00:15:17.047 --> 00:15:22.786
<i>If his bio tech tail isn't repulsive
enough, he also shoots acid venom.</i>


00:15:25.488 --> 00:15:27.391
Say hello, Copperhead.


00:15:32.796 --> 00:15:36.600
The last is Bronze Tiger,
AKA Ben Turner.


00:15:37.568 --> 00:15:40.438
<i>Ex-CIA, then vigilante.</i>


00:15:41.973 --> 00:15:45.476
<i>Possibly the greatest
martial artist in the world.</i>


00:15:48.711 --> 00:15:54.649
If it weren't for his vow never to take
an innocent life, I'd put him incharge.


00:16:00.223 --> 00:16:02.260
I can feel the love.


00:16:13.804 --> 00:16:15.202
Open wide, Ms. Frost.


00:16:15.204 --> 00:16:16.605
Bite me.


00:16:19.377 --> 00:16:21.910
Thank you. Try not to move.


00:16:21.912 --> 00:16:24.914
We wouldn't want the appartus
to go off accidentally.


00:16:24.916 --> 00:16:27.082
It happened once
to the ten-eyed man.


00:16:27.084 --> 00:16:28.319
Who?


00:16:28.852 --> 00:16:30.421
Exactly.


00:16:50.306 --> 00:16:52.207
Insertion's complete.


00:16:52.209 --> 00:16:53.810
Task force X is
locked and loaded.


00:16:57.547 --> 00:16:59.614
Woo-hoo!


00:16:59.616 --> 00:17:01.419
What's this all about, Waller?


00:17:02.451 --> 00:17:05.053
This is about making me
happy, Tiger.


00:17:05.055 --> 00:17:07.557
This time I'm searching
for something special.


00:17:08.258 --> 00:17:10.959
A lost card.


00:17:10.961 --> 00:17:14.295
Just call the bank, honey.
They'll get you a new one.


00:17:14.297 --> 00:17:16.566
What's it got?
Some kind of code?


00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:18.867
You might say.


00:17:18.869 --> 00:17:21.736
The last person who had it
was this man.


00:17:21.738 --> 00:17:24.475
He calls himself "Steel Maxim."


00:17:25.275 --> 00:17:27.441
Seriously?


00:17:27.443 --> 00:17:31.646
<i>Late 20s, no distinguishing
marks, except for a tramp stamp.</i>


00:17:31.648 --> 00:17:33.180
<i>An Egyptian Ankh.</i>


00:17:33.182 --> 00:17:36.316
We think he played a part
in the card's disappearance.


00:17:36.318 --> 00:17:38.821
But he's been hard
to track down.


00:17:38.823 --> 00:17:43.057
Find him, and I'll slice a year
of all your sentences.


00:17:43.059 --> 00:17:46.960
Oh, great, only 87 more
suicide missions to go.


00:17:46.962 --> 00:17:47.998
Cheers, Waller.


00:17:49.799 --> 00:17:51.632
One more thing.


00:17:51.634 --> 00:17:53.534
This one's off the grid.


00:17:53.536 --> 00:17:56.737
You'll be dealing with me
directly and only me.


00:17:56.739 --> 00:17:59.006
Deadshot will be
your team leader.


00:17:59.008 --> 00:18:03.178
I told you before, Waller, I don't
take orders from murderers.


00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:05.548
Not even if I said, "Please"?


00:18:07.485 --> 00:18:10.919
I answer to a higher authority.


00:18:10.921 --> 00:18:14.922
Higher than Waller? That
sounds like blasphemy, mate.


00:18:14.924 --> 00:18:18.059
I'd say maybe we should
take this outside.


00:18:18.061 --> 00:18:19.660
But that's up to her.


00:18:19.662 --> 00:18:21.295
Settle down, love birds.


00:18:21.297 --> 00:18:24.334
It's too early to start
losing your heads just yet.


00:18:26.236 --> 00:18:29.073
I've requisitioned
this vehicle for your mission.


00:18:30.874 --> 00:18:32.707
You're kidding?


00:18:32.709 --> 00:18:35.912
Like I said,
this one is off the books.


00:18:37.081 --> 00:18:38.379
No hotels...


00:18:38.381 --> 00:18:41.249
Roadtrip!


00:18:41.251 --> 00:18:45.088
I guess that'll save us from having
to explain him to the concierge.


00:18:46.757 --> 00:18:47.958
Hiss.


00:18:49.492 --> 00:18:52.929
Hey, we got cheese dogs
and Chicken Nuggies!


00:18:54.864 --> 00:18:56.566
Blow me up now.


00:20:04.434 --> 00:20:06.002
It's about time.


00:20:06.937 --> 00:20:09.571
Your late, you waste of flesh.


00:20:09.573 --> 00:20:13.544
Banshee, is that any way
to talk to our associate?


00:20:16.013 --> 00:20:18.749
Please, see him in.


00:20:20.083 --> 00:20:22.382
Word is, they gave her
six months tops,


00:20:22.384 --> 00:20:24.319
so really wants the card
bad now.


00:20:24.321 --> 00:20:28.025
It's all there, all the information
Waller has on the card.


00:20:29.093 --> 00:20:32.393
Your text said
she sent out Task Force X.


00:20:32.395 --> 00:20:34.227
Last night,


00:20:34.229 --> 00:20:36.531
I tried to get these to you
sooner, but I have to be careful.


00:20:36.533 --> 00:20:39.301
The Wall has eyes everywhere.


00:20:39.303 --> 00:20:40.970
I shouldn't be gone too long.


00:20:45.142 --> 00:20:47.374
Uh, thanks.


00:20:47.376 --> 00:20:52.182
Before you rush off, you neglected to
tell me where Waller is sending them.


00:20:53.049 --> 00:20:54.948
Branson.


00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:57.217
The man they're tracking, he's been
spotted there looking for work.


00:20:57.219 --> 00:20:58.622
What does he do?


00:20:59.322 --> 00:21:00.690
He's an...


00:21:01.592 --> 00:21:03.060
entertainer.


00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:16.840
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.
- Hey!


00:21:20.177 --> 00:21:21.545
Park in the back.


00:21:28.918 --> 00:21:31.155
Oh, yeah, whoo!


00:21:41.698 --> 00:21:44.166
- Woo-hoo, yeah!
- Curb it, clown.


00:21:44.168 --> 00:21:46.668
We don't wanna call attention
to ourselves.


00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:51.473
Honey, in case you haven't
noticed, nobody's looking at us.


00:21:51.475 --> 00:21:53.774
- Split up.
- Dibs on backstage!


00:21:53.776 --> 00:21:55.813
Woo-hoo. I like that!


00:21:58.148 --> 00:21:59.617
I'm going.


00:22:06.556 --> 00:22:09.189
Look at the bag of marbles
on that fella.


00:22:09.191 --> 00:22:12.962
You missed your calling, Snake eyes,
chicks would go crazy for you.


00:22:13.796 --> 00:22:16.931
Bored now. Going out.


00:22:16.933 --> 00:22:19.400
Uh-uh, we're on standby.


00:22:19.402 --> 00:22:21.201
Deadshot gave us montior duty.


00:22:21.203 --> 00:22:24.339
So much for not taking orders
from murderers, eh, Benji?


00:22:24.341 --> 00:22:26.108
Shut it, Boomer.


00:22:26.110 --> 00:22:27.745
Sit your ass down.


00:22:28.478 --> 00:22:30.314
Make me, dolomite.


00:22:33.049 --> 00:22:34.949
I don't kill innocents.


00:22:34.951 --> 00:22:36.921
But I doubt if you'd qualify.


00:22:38.555 --> 00:22:40.088
Pull it back.


00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:41.992
Or I'll rip your mouth in half.


00:22:48.798 --> 00:22:51.032
You're on a mission,


00:22:51.034 --> 00:22:55.738
you don't wander away, you don't make
trouble, and you don't piss me off.


00:23:09.251 --> 00:23:11.151
We didn't see him.


00:23:11.153 --> 00:23:12.919
This nut job was
frisking the boys.


00:23:12.921 --> 00:23:15.623
I had to cool her off.


00:23:15.625 --> 00:23:18.092
Psychotics have needs, you know?


00:23:18.094 --> 00:23:19.630
We have needs.


00:23:21.463 --> 00:23:23.066
We're moving to the next club.


00:23:23.967 --> 00:23:25.766
This is gonna take forever.


00:23:25.768 --> 00:23:28.669
Well, we could always
put up some flyers.


00:23:28.671 --> 00:23:33.975
<i>Ladies and ladies,
it's that king from Cairo,</i>


00:23:33.977 --> 00:23:36.276
<i>the sphinx of kinks,</i>


00:23:36.278 --> 00:23:42.251
<i>the sandstorm guaranteed
to blow you away.</i>


00:23:42.986 --> 00:23:44.852
Oh!


00:23:44.854 --> 00:23:49.657
<i>Get ready to sweat
for the Pharaoh!</i>


00:23:55.931 --> 00:23:57.735
Didn't see him backstage.


00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:00.003
Me likey.


00:24:30.799 --> 00:24:32.036
It's him.


00:24:47.450 --> 00:24:50.187
- Banshee! Oh, crap!
- Where're you going?


00:24:56.392 --> 00:24:57.428
Shit!


00:24:58.828 --> 00:25:01.364
Oh, crap! Oh, crap!
Oh, crap! Oh, crap!


00:25:25.721 --> 00:25:27.156
Uh. No!


00:25:50.346 --> 00:25:52.215
No!


00:25:57.321 --> 00:25:59.055
Oh, this is bad.


00:26:31.054 --> 00:26:32.322
Buddy Frankenstein?


00:26:47.638 --> 00:26:49.072
Whoa!


00:27:02.051 --> 00:27:04.288
Zoom, what the hell?


00:27:05.153 --> 00:27:07.155
What are you waiting for?


00:27:07.157 --> 00:27:09.193
Do I have to do everything?


00:27:14.998 --> 00:27:18.134
Hiya, cowboy, need a ride?


00:27:28.978 --> 00:27:30.346
Get us out of here!


00:27:40.324 --> 00:27:41.456
Heads up, mate.


00:27:42.659 --> 00:27:44.494
<i>Ha ha. Right in the gulleys.</i>


00:28:10.553 --> 00:28:13.254
- Something's wrong.
- Yeah, he's too fast for him.


00:28:13.256 --> 00:28:15.255
No, he's too slow.


00:28:15.257 --> 00:28:18.927
He should've broken into this
jalopy and killed us all by now.


00:28:18.929 --> 00:28:20.130
He's still mine.


00:28:25.834 --> 00:28:27.237
Frost, on the right!


00:28:44.554 --> 00:28:48.822
Pfft. Come on. You don't understand.
I've got a 10:00 a.m. call back


00:28:48.824 --> 00:28:50.225
<i>for Bachelor Babe.</i>


00:28:50.227 --> 00:28:52.826
Really? Aw, that's
my favorite show.


00:28:52.828 --> 00:28:57.331
It's so romantic like you're
the only girl at a frat party.


00:28:57.333 --> 00:29:01.169
Oh, you're not going anywhere,
buddy, until we get some answers.


00:29:01.171 --> 00:29:03.470
Like why're you
so popular with Zoom?


00:29:03.472 --> 00:29:05.840
How should I know?
I've never even seen the guy.


00:29:05.842 --> 00:29:07.809
But you knew Silver Banshee.


00:29:07.811 --> 00:29:10.277
The second you saw her,
you bolted.


00:29:10.279 --> 00:29:13.014
Yeah, everyone knows who
Silver Banshee is.


00:29:13.016 --> 00:29:15.115
Uh, no.


00:29:15.117 --> 00:29:19.253
Okay, okay, so we crossed
paths a few times. So what?


00:29:19.255 --> 00:29:20.987
Listen to this tosser.


00:29:20.989 --> 00:29:23.724
How'd a nobody like you
even get Banshee's attention?


00:29:23.726 --> 00:29:25.529
Because I was Fate.


00:29:27.430 --> 00:29:29.764
Dr. Fate. I used to be
Dr. Fate, okay?


00:29:29.766 --> 00:29:31.832
Shut up.


00:29:31.834 --> 00:29:34.834
It's true. It's not like
I was the only one.


00:29:34.836 --> 00:29:36.303
There have been a lot of Fates.


00:29:36.305 --> 00:29:38.406
Uh, they're chosen by
the spirit of Nabu.


00:29:38.408 --> 00:29:40.809
Oh, yeah?
Why'd he choose you?


00:29:40.811 --> 00:29:42.476
Uh, why not me?


00:29:42.478 --> 00:29:44.579
Six percent body fat,
20 inch guns.


00:29:44.581 --> 00:29:46.913
Hell, I even took
a magic class once.


00:29:46.915 --> 00:29:51.284
<i>So, I was going strong at the end
of this 10k when I saw it, uh...</i>


00:29:51.286 --> 00:29:52.355
him.


00:29:53.990 --> 00:29:56.325
<i>And at first,
I thought he was God.</i>


00:29:58.227 --> 00:30:00.564
<i>I just couldn't figure
what religion.</i>


00:30:02.532 --> 00:30:06.368
<i>And Nabu wasn't much of a talker
but when I had that helmet on,</i>


00:30:06.370 --> 00:30:09.137
<i>it was like, I didn't need
to hear him at all.</i>


00:30:09.139 --> 00:30:12.640
<i>Like, I knew what to do.</i>


00:30:12.642 --> 00:30:15.810
<i>Let me tell you,
I was hella hot.</i>


00:30:15.812 --> 00:30:18.412
<i>Superhero-hot.</i>


00:30:18.414 --> 00:30:22.151
<i>Banshee was sprung as soon
as she laid eyes on moi.</i>


00:30:29.290 --> 00:30:33.761
<i>I mean, come on. Sure she
played hard to get at first.</i>


00:30:33.763 --> 00:30:36.433
<i>But I know that
she knew what was up.</i>


00:30:38.034 --> 00:30:39.268
<i>Oh, she knew.</i>


00:30:40.436 --> 00:30:42.506
<i>Oh, yeah.
She knew.</i>


00:30:44.073 --> 00:30:46.306
Oh, my God, they did it.


00:30:46.308 --> 00:30:48.976
That was sweet day.


00:30:48.978 --> 00:30:51.411
<i>I mean, Nabu hooked me up
with my own place.</i>


00:30:51.413 --> 00:30:53.746
<i>Sometimes I'd have to
fight off hell dogs,</i>


00:30:53.748 --> 00:30:56.115
<i>and you know,
some crazy demons.</i>


00:30:56.117 --> 00:30:59.352
<i>But I spent most of the time
dusting his knick-knacks.</i>


00:30:59.354 --> 00:31:01.757
<i>This dude had everything
but a dead monkey.</i>


00:31:04.260 --> 00:31:06.459
<i>But of all the junk,
the thing that Nabu cherished</i>


00:31:06.461 --> 00:31:09.098
<i>the absolute most
was the smallest.</i>


00:31:12.067 --> 00:31:14.333
<i>A shiny black card.</i>


00:31:14.335 --> 00:31:16.169
<i>It had writing on it.</i>


00:31:18.940 --> 00:31:20.873
<i>"Get out of hell free?"</i>


00:31:20.875 --> 00:31:23.910
It's crazy, I know, I read about
it in one of Nabu's books.


00:31:23.912 --> 00:31:27.281
Supposedly, if you have this
card on you when you die,


00:31:27.283 --> 00:31:29.786
you bypass hell and
you go straight to heaven.


00:31:31.754 --> 00:31:33.486
Oh, like a DFA pass.


00:31:33.488 --> 00:31:35.857
Yeah.


00:31:35.859 --> 00:31:39.226
A whole lot of blood should we
start to have a card like that.


00:31:39.228 --> 00:31:44.732
Yeah, but only one person can
use it, then it's used up.


00:31:44.734 --> 00:31:48.870
All I know is that damn card
screwed up my situation for good.


00:31:48.872 --> 00:31:50.437
What do you mean?


00:31:50.439 --> 00:31:52.872
I'd been there about
two months, and it gets old.


00:31:52.874 --> 00:31:57.477
<i>So one evening, I hit this bar
and I meet this redhead.</i>


00:31:57.479 --> 00:32:00.147
<i>And she's so hot.
So I said to her...</i>


00:32:00.149 --> 00:32:03.386
You don't know it yet, baby,
but you just met your fate.


00:32:06.221 --> 00:32:08.523
<i>Cornball? Yes, but it works.</i>


00:32:08.525 --> 00:32:11.128
<i>Especially when I bring her
back to my place.</i>


00:32:12.761 --> 00:32:15.196
<i>She had this girlfriend
with her, kinda hard and quiet,</i>


00:32:15.198 --> 00:32:18.399
<i>not really my type but
they were a package deal.</i>


00:32:18.401 --> 00:32:20.336
<i>Like I'm gonna say no to that?</i>


00:32:21.937 --> 00:32:24.405
<i>It started off great.</i>


00:32:24.407 --> 00:32:27.774
<i>But after a while,
I got a little suspicious</i>


00:32:27.776 --> 00:32:30.544
<i>'cause the butch one hadn't
joined in the fun yet.</i>


00:32:30.546 --> 00:32:33.346
<i>I mean, who can say no
to all of this. Am I right?</i>


00:32:33.348 --> 00:32:38.252
<i>And I catch her red-handed
boosting the freaking card.</i>


00:32:38.254 --> 00:32:39.689
<i>I mean, who does that?</i>


00:33:07.749 --> 00:33:10.386
<i>And the only thing they took
was the card.</i>


00:33:12.488 --> 00:33:14.524
<i>Everything else was untouched.</i>


00:33:16.359 --> 00:33:17.827
<i>Including me.</i>


00:33:19.062 --> 00:33:20.664
<i>You think he cared?</i>


00:33:26.736 --> 00:33:28.972
<i>He didn't even give me
a chance to explain.</i>


00:33:30.973 --> 00:33:35.642
A couple of days later, I called up
my girlfriend, and she was freaking.


00:33:35.644 --> 00:33:37.878
She said people were looking
for me, government types.


00:33:37.880 --> 00:33:40.281
They were asking about the card.
Like I knew where it was.


00:33:40.283 --> 00:33:44.485
Anyway, she blocked me, so I called
up my sidechick, same thing.


00:33:44.487 --> 00:33:47.153
Finally, I ran out of options.


00:33:47.155 --> 00:33:51.824
So I changed my name and have
been lying low ever since.


00:33:51.826 --> 00:33:55.195
Calling yourself "Steel Maxim,"
and stripping.


00:33:55.197 --> 00:33:56.996
That's lying low to you?


00:33:56.998 --> 00:34:01.768
It's called hiding
in plain sight, sweetheart.


00:34:01.770 --> 00:34:04.237
Anyway, you gotta believe me,
I had nothing to do


00:34:04.239 --> 00:34:07.809
with the card,
I swear on my life!


00:34:07.811 --> 00:34:09.643
<i>So who's Dr. Fate now?</i>


00:34:09.645 --> 00:34:11.377
<i>I heard Nabu
picked some chick.</i>


00:34:11.379 --> 00:34:13.647
You get all that?


00:34:13.649 --> 00:34:16.286
I got it.
He's telling the truth.


00:34:16.785 --> 00:34:18.719
Useless.


00:34:18.721 --> 00:34:21.422
But at least now,
we know who took the card.


00:34:21.424 --> 00:34:24.525
Sounded like Scandal Savage
and Knockout.


00:34:24.527 --> 00:34:26.960
But it didn't sound like
their kind of heist.


00:34:26.962 --> 00:34:28.495
It's not.


00:34:28.497 --> 00:34:31.899
I bet my eyeteeth that her daddy
Vandal Savage is on this.


00:34:31.901 --> 00:34:34.034
According to
the Justice League database,


00:34:34.036 --> 00:34:37.437
that bastard is
a 50,000 year old caveman


00:34:37.439 --> 00:34:40.542
<i>who was affected by radiation
from a meteorite.</i>


00:34:41.277 --> 00:34:42.909
<i>Yeah, I know.</i>


00:34:42.911 --> 00:34:46.679
Anyway, you might be familiar
with his other nom de plume.


00:34:46.681 --> 00:34:51.484
<i>Alexander the Great, Caesar,
Genghis Khan.</i>


00:34:51.486 --> 00:34:54.721
He's history's bloodiest tyrant.


00:34:54.723 --> 00:34:56.790
And you're going after him.


00:34:56.792 --> 00:35:01.395
Whoa, whoa, whoa, I didn't signup
to deal with an immortal butcher.


00:35:01.397 --> 00:35:03.330
You didn't sign up for anything.


00:35:03.332 --> 00:35:07.304
I run the op the way I want,
and I want that card, Deadshot.


00:35:10.272 --> 00:35:12.672
I need it.


00:35:12.674 --> 00:35:15.743
It's Savage, Waller,
you gotta give me something.


00:35:15.745 --> 00:35:17.745
But we already have Zoom
on our ass.


00:35:17.747 --> 00:35:19.683
I can't go back to them
with nothing.


00:35:20.850 --> 00:35:22.815
Fine. Ten years.


00:35:22.817 --> 00:35:25.453
I'll give you ten years off.


00:35:25.455 --> 00:35:27.620
You know what that
means for you?


00:35:27.622 --> 00:35:28.891
You're out.


00:35:30.259 --> 00:35:31.661
If you're in...


00:35:39.569 --> 00:35:41.538
So when do we get the show
on the road?


00:35:44.073 --> 00:35:45.374
Drive.


00:35:54.450 --> 00:35:56.453
What do we do
with Magic Mike?


00:36:03.593 --> 00:36:05.562
Hey!


00:36:07.428 --> 00:36:08.929
Not cool.


00:36:08.931 --> 00:36:11.868
At least you could call me
a car, assholes.


00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:45.699
Which exit, cowboy?


00:36:45.701 --> 00:36:49.270
Waller said to keep going
north until we hear from her.


00:36:49.272 --> 00:36:51.605
I'm surprised she really
believes this mumbo-jumbo.


00:36:51.607 --> 00:36:53.107
- Do you?
- What?


00:36:53.109 --> 00:36:55.408
You know, that
you can skip hell.


00:36:55.410 --> 00:36:59.614
Beats me. I always thought
this was hell, Captain Kangaroo.


00:36:59.616 --> 00:37:02.150
Hey, all right.
First up, that's offensive.


00:37:02.152 --> 00:37:03.683
I'll tell you another thing.


00:37:03.685 --> 00:37:06.487
If any of us truly
deserves hell, it's Waller.


00:37:06.489 --> 00:37:07.821
And that bitch knows it.


00:37:07.823 --> 00:37:09.623
My God, the way she does.


00:37:09.625 --> 00:37:12.659
I ain't worrying. I know
I'm going to heaven.


00:37:12.661 --> 00:37:16.797
Anyone who can put up with
Mr. J deserves a break.


00:37:16.799 --> 00:37:19.266
The problem is, sweetheart,


00:37:19.268 --> 00:37:22.703
you have to die in order to find
out if the card really works.


00:37:22.705 --> 00:37:24.804
Pretty-bloody-embarrassing
if it didn't.


00:37:24.806 --> 00:37:26.806
What about you, gunman?


00:37:26.808 --> 00:37:29.609
You think the card will work
like the blood you spilled?


00:37:29.611 --> 00:37:31.779
Or don't you believe in heaven?


00:37:31.781 --> 00:37:33.650
I believe in heaven, Boomer.


00:37:35.218 --> 00:37:37.020
Everytime you shut your mouth.


00:37:39.756 --> 00:37:42.388
You joke about heaven
and hell, Deadshot.


00:37:42.390 --> 00:37:45.759
But trust me, they exist.


00:37:45.761 --> 00:37:48.529
There's not a morning goes by
I don't get up wondering


00:37:48.531 --> 00:37:50.567
if this will be
my judgement day.


00:37:51.466 --> 00:37:54.167
Lined up with the woman I love.


00:37:54.169 --> 00:37:57.973
Will face the lake of hell fire with
the same vermin who brought me down.


00:38:00.509 --> 00:38:04.178
The only thing any of us can
hope for is divine intervention.


00:38:04.180 --> 00:38:08.915
Only through the grace of God can
we be saved from eternal damnation.


00:38:08.917 --> 00:38:11.153
For all the blood we spilt...


00:38:13.022 --> 00:38:16.558
Everything else is just talk.


00:38:23.232 --> 00:38:25.735
So, guess the card
couldn't hurt then, eh?


00:38:31.272 --> 00:38:34.275
Dude, this is
the way they left me.


00:38:34.277 --> 00:38:35.609
I was kidnapped.


00:38:35.611 --> 00:38:37.377
Thats's what they all
say, buddy.


00:38:37.379 --> 00:38:39.545
We'll get you something pretty
to wear back at the station.


00:38:39.547 --> 00:38:41.049
Hope you like pink.


00:38:45.754 --> 00:38:48.254
Sorry, officer.


00:38:48.256 --> 00:38:51.093
But I think your tags
are about to expire.


00:38:51.727 --> 00:38:53.096
Oh, crap.


00:38:56.165 --> 00:38:58.464
<i>All right,
listen up, it turns out</i>


00:38:58.466 --> 00:39:02.335
<i>that Scandal Savage and her gal
pal have an apartment in Denver.</i>


00:39:02.337 --> 00:39:05.941
<i>There's a hidden safe. I'll
be sending you floor plans.</i>


00:39:09.978 --> 00:39:12.179
Yes, sir. We'll be ready.


00:39:12.181 --> 00:39:13.880
Wonderful.


00:39:13.882 --> 00:39:18.484
A few days without a scalpel in my
hand, I'll start to feel all fidgety.


00:39:18.486 --> 00:39:21.554
Better get dressed, babe.
The caveman cometh.


00:39:21.556 --> 00:39:24.960
Oh, about time. This little
piggy's been cramping our style.


00:39:28.631 --> 00:39:30.362
No peeking.


00:39:30.364 --> 00:39:33.000
Madam, I'm a surgeon.


00:39:33.002 --> 00:39:35.902
I've seen bodies before.


00:39:35.904 --> 00:39:37.339
Not like this one.


00:40:29.123 --> 00:40:30.627
Fun!


00:40:44.339 --> 00:40:48.975
I don't know why your papa wants me
for a job any bone cutter could do.


00:40:48.977 --> 00:40:53.078
My work is art,
it's transformational.


00:40:53.080 --> 00:40:55.982
So is your bank account
if you do this right.


00:40:55.984 --> 00:40:59.018
I have been wanting this
since I escaped from Apocalypse.


00:40:59.020 --> 00:41:01.790
Hmm, what do you think?
Too Wonder Woman?


00:41:02.524 --> 00:41:04.794
He likes Wonder Woman.


00:41:05.627 --> 00:41:07.226
There's only three.


00:41:07.228 --> 00:41:10.198
Some guy in cuffs
and a pig mask.


00:41:10.700 --> 00:41:11.933
Kinky.


00:41:15.238 --> 00:41:17.674
They usually call up
first, don't they?


00:41:54.076 --> 00:41:55.911
Oh, God!


00:42:00.783 --> 00:42:02.819
I smell bacon.


00:42:04.520 --> 00:42:05.822
You heard me.


00:42:14.596 --> 00:42:16.362
So far no one's died.


00:42:16.364 --> 00:42:18.868
Let's see how long
we can make that last.


00:42:24.906 --> 00:42:26.441
Now.


00:42:31.712 --> 00:42:33.212
It's here.


00:42:33.214 --> 00:42:35.949
Frost, how about a few
icy cuffs for the ladies?


00:43:00.241 --> 00:43:01.377
Balls.


00:43:30.172 --> 00:43:31.908
What a world. What a world!


00:43:43.718 --> 00:43:45.652
We can't get a clean shot.


00:43:45.654 --> 00:43:48.024
The woman is expendable.


00:44:52.219 --> 00:44:56.690
I know you could see me, Savage,
I got the card!


00:44:56.692 --> 00:44:58.225
You really want to kill me?


00:44:58.227 --> 00:45:00.326
I'm guessing no,
but then again,


00:45:00.328 --> 00:45:03.098
but who'd have guessed
a caveman believed in hell?


00:45:13.274 --> 00:45:14.908
Everyone, get behind me.


00:45:14.910 --> 00:45:16.344
No fast moves.


00:45:18.881 --> 00:45:20.913
Can't negotiate with him.


00:45:20.915 --> 00:45:25.419
Right now, we're just playing
poker, and I've got the wild card.


00:45:25.421 --> 00:45:27.623
Well, that makes me feel
a lot better.


00:45:32.259 --> 00:45:34.194
Father, we must help her.


00:45:34.196 --> 00:45:35.964
Get Pyg onboard.


00:45:36.964 --> 00:45:39.000
She's dying, she can't be left.


00:45:46.774 --> 00:45:48.143
Get Pyg.


00:45:52.413 --> 00:45:55.181
Christ, I thought
you were a lousy father.


00:45:55.183 --> 00:45:57.585
Just move back nice and slow.


00:46:04.759 --> 00:46:07.060
We're like fish
in a freaking barrel.


00:46:07.062 --> 00:46:10.630
If you kill me,
your card gets used up.


00:46:10.632 --> 00:46:14.466
If you wound me,
my friends will finish the job.


00:46:14.468 --> 00:46:18.672
Either way, you lose
your ticket to heaven.


00:46:18.674 --> 00:46:23.379
Give me the card, and I'll
spare all your sorry lives.


00:46:24.046 --> 00:46:25.612
Sounds reasonable.


00:46:25.614 --> 00:46:27.047
We're so screwed.


00:46:27.049 --> 00:46:28.417
Okay.


00:46:32.721 --> 00:46:33.989
Oh, come on.


00:46:42.564 --> 00:46:44.533
You better be up there
snake man.


00:47:38.721 --> 00:47:42.890
Gee, Frosty, it's like
Christmas eveyday with you.


00:47:53.569 --> 00:47:56.572
Trust me, that one's
out of order.


00:48:13.022 --> 00:48:14.757
Damn it, we're too late.


00:48:16.658 --> 00:48:18.958
So they didn't get the card.


00:48:18.960 --> 00:48:21.761
At least we know who's got it.


00:48:21.763 --> 00:48:24.496
Savage has disappeared
for decades.


00:48:24.498 --> 00:48:26.267
I can't lose them.


00:49:10.946 --> 00:49:13.446
<i>I understand he took you
by surprise.</i>


00:49:13.448 --> 00:49:19.518
<i>What I don't understand is why I'm not
blowing your fool heads off right now.</i>


00:49:19.520 --> 00:49:22.321
His ship was as big as a 747.


00:49:22.323 --> 00:49:24.924
Your satellite's must've
picked him up.


00:49:24.926 --> 00:49:26.893
<i>Savage uses a cloaking device.</i>


00:49:26.895 --> 00:49:28.862
<i>He could hide the moon
if he wanted to.</i>


00:49:28.864 --> 00:49:31.198
He must've left
some kind of trail.


00:49:31.200 --> 00:49:33.533
A heat signature?
A disruption in the clouds?


00:49:33.535 --> 00:49:35.567
<i>You better hope
we find something.</i>


00:49:35.569 --> 00:49:39.237
<i>Otherwise, this camping trip
is over.</i>


00:49:39.239 --> 00:49:41.140
<i>Waller out.</i>


00:49:41.142 --> 00:49:44.143
Oh, Benji gets a star.


00:49:44.145 --> 00:49:45.877
We should've kept on fighting.


00:49:45.879 --> 00:49:48.183
At least one of us would've
gotten out with a card.


00:49:49.216 --> 00:49:51.016
Hey, where you going?


00:49:51.018 --> 00:49:52.451
I need to get some air.


00:49:52.453 --> 00:49:54.455
Well, who's gonna lead us?


00:49:55.323 --> 00:49:56.859
You're incharge.


00:50:03.364 --> 00:50:05.534
Who wants pizza?


00:50:35.364 --> 00:50:37.263
It's okay.


00:50:37.265 --> 00:50:38.700
I'm looking for Zoe.


00:50:39.399 --> 00:50:41.234
Are you her dad?


00:50:41.236 --> 00:50:42.538
Yeah.


00:50:44.306 --> 00:50:45.808
Where are you guns?


00:50:51.046 --> 00:50:53.513
Cool. A lot of .45s right?


00:50:53.515 --> 00:50:55.815
I play a lot of
first person shooters.


00:50:55.817 --> 00:50:57.886
<i>I'm PussycatKill
on Blood World.</i>


00:50:59.988 --> 00:51:01.654
Why isn't she here?


00:51:01.656 --> 00:51:03.424
She stays away a lot.


00:51:04.259 --> 00:51:06.027
Crap. You got any?


00:51:07.127 --> 00:51:08.694
Where'd she go?


00:51:08.696 --> 00:51:11.596
Southside on King street,
There's a drug house.


00:51:11.598 --> 00:51:13.334
She usually ends up there.


00:51:14.868 --> 00:51:17.435
Don't get me wrong.
She's no tweaker.


00:51:17.437 --> 00:51:19.406
Maybe some weed.


00:51:19.408 --> 00:51:23.241
Speaking of, might as well
wake and bake since I'm up.


00:51:23.243 --> 00:51:25.011
She says she's like you.


00:51:25.013 --> 00:51:26.882
Likes to live dangerously.


00:51:28.183 --> 00:51:30.984
But she kind of hates you too.


00:51:30.986 --> 00:51:33.989
I asked my therapist about it,
but he was already asleep.


00:51:35.089 --> 00:51:36.325
Want some?


00:51:38.160 --> 00:51:39.395
More for me.


00:52:13.027 --> 00:52:14.962
Seen her around here lately?


00:52:15.997 --> 00:52:17.629
Sorry.


00:52:17.631 --> 00:52:19.565
You lonely, darling?


00:52:19.567 --> 00:52:21.669
No, thanks,
I'm just looking for...


00:52:22.603 --> 00:52:25.440
Zoe?


00:52:31.111 --> 00:52:34.349
Hey, hey, hey.
What's your hurry, buddy?


00:52:36.185 --> 00:52:38.752
Tough guy, huh? He got any cash?


00:52:38.754 --> 00:52:42.357
Look, you dickless wonders,
I don't have time for this.


00:52:45.426 --> 00:52:47.462
You're in trouble, deadbeat.


00:52:48.696 --> 00:52:50.798
You shut off your comm lines.


00:52:56.270 --> 00:52:58.106
Your kid's not on mission.


00:52:59.174 --> 00:53:00.841
You don't understand.


00:53:00.843 --> 00:53:03.643
You think you're the only one
who's lost someone?


00:53:03.645 --> 00:53:05.612
Remember
the League of Assassins?


00:53:05.614 --> 00:53:08.480
You worked for 'em
once or twice.


00:53:08.482 --> 00:53:11.085
Once. Lousy benefits.


00:53:15.056 --> 00:53:18.024
Went undercover and
infiltrated them the agency.


00:53:18.026 --> 00:53:20.826
They found out,
they tried to kill me,


00:53:20.828 --> 00:53:22.864
but that's easier said
than done.


00:53:23.864 --> 00:53:26.435
<i>So they went after my fiance.</i>


00:53:30.906 --> 00:53:35.141
<i>I tracked down and killed
as many of them I could.</i>


00:53:35.143 --> 00:53:38.444
<i>Including a few moles
working for us.</i>


00:53:38.446 --> 00:53:43.786
I didn't know, but to tell you
the truth, I didn't care.


00:53:44.518 --> 00:53:46.620
This story have a point?


00:53:46.622 --> 00:53:50.422
Don't make me feel sorry for
you and your rathole existence.


00:53:50.424 --> 00:53:54.194
I did everything in God's power
to protect the woman I loved.


00:53:54.196 --> 00:53:56.799
But you, you threw
your daughter away.


00:54:15.384 --> 00:54:16.652
Shit.


00:54:35.770 --> 00:54:37.605
I was holding back
because of your kid,


00:54:39.308 --> 00:54:40.909
but now I'm gonna finish this.


00:54:43.578 --> 00:54:45.712
Deadshot, you gotta
call the Wall.


00:54:45.714 --> 00:54:48.480
She went nuts when
she found out I was incharge.


00:54:48.482 --> 00:54:52.217
I says to her, "So how's a girl
supposed to get ahead in this outfit?"


00:54:52.219 --> 00:54:54.857
And that's when she got
really pissed off.


00:54:55.390 --> 00:54:56.725
Shall we?


00:54:59.426 --> 00:55:00.761
It's not her.


00:55:12.339 --> 00:55:14.839
I'm here.


00:55:14.841 --> 00:55:17.609
<i>You're one lucky guy, Lawton.</i>


00:55:17.611 --> 00:55:22.084
<i>You don't know how close you came
to an out-of-body experience.</i>


00:55:22.850 --> 00:55:25.884
I took a side trip. So what?


00:55:25.886 --> 00:55:27.622
Tiger's incharge.


00:55:29.424 --> 00:55:30.626
You heard the woman.


00:55:31.326 --> 00:55:32.561
Drive.


00:55:48.209 --> 00:55:50.710
Waller wants us to keep going
north for the time being.


00:55:50.712 --> 00:55:54.716
We'll take a rest stop here
and reconvene at 1700 hours.


00:55:57.417 --> 00:55:58.719
Five o' clock.


00:56:00.187 --> 00:56:01.189
Oh!


00:56:07.661 --> 00:56:09.765
I think grumpy's staying.


00:56:10.931 --> 00:56:12.801
Are you stayin' grumpy?


00:56:14.968 --> 00:56:17.138
Yep, grumpy's staying.


00:56:21.143 --> 00:56:23.810
I'm gonna order some food.
What do you want?


00:56:23.812 --> 00:56:26.014
Anything but chicken nuggies.


00:56:26.980 --> 00:56:28.584
I'm going to the can.


00:56:30.518 --> 00:56:32.754
I bet she pees icicles.


00:56:47.935 --> 00:56:49.203
Hmm.


00:56:56.310 --> 00:56:58.078
Who is this?


00:56:58.080 --> 00:57:00.413
<i>Listen clsoe, 'cause
I'm only gonna say this once.</i>


00:57:00.415 --> 00:57:04.953
32.1 degrees north,
minus 112 degrees east.


00:58:02.343 --> 00:58:03.678
What the hell?


00:58:05.946 --> 00:58:08.915
<i>- And no onions.
- Tiger.</i>


00:58:08.917 --> 00:58:11.384
<i>- They got Frost.
- What?</i>


00:58:11.386 --> 00:58:12.788
I'm goin' after them.


00:59:53.988 --> 00:59:55.857
<i>Hope you're doing all right.</i>


00:59:58.192 --> 01:00:00.692
Sorry if Banshee
got a little rough.


01:00:00.694 --> 01:00:02.194
She feels terrible.


01:00:02.196 --> 01:00:05.566
Yeah, I'm all up in
my feelings about it.


01:00:08.904 --> 01:00:11.536
Honestly, we meant you no harm.


01:00:11.538 --> 01:00:12.973
We just want to talk.


01:00:14.542 --> 01:00:17.844
Fact is, I'm a fan.


01:00:17.846 --> 01:00:22.281
I mean, this gift you have,
it's really quite extraordinary.


01:00:22.283 --> 01:00:25.286
I don't think people realize
what you're capable of doing.


01:00:26.286 --> 01:00:27.955
What's this about?


01:00:29.924 --> 01:00:32.257
Its about a favor.


01:00:32.259 --> 01:00:34.560
Everyone needs a favor
once in a while.


01:00:34.562 --> 01:00:37.096
Banshee here would like me
to help her go back in time


01:00:37.098 --> 01:00:39.899
to seek vengeance against
the clan who banished her.


01:00:39.901 --> 01:00:41.201
That bastards!


01:00:41.203 --> 01:00:44.536
Blockbuster, uncomplicated
fellow that he is


01:00:44.538 --> 01:00:46.471
would like his own island.


01:00:48.975 --> 01:00:51.844
Me? I want the card.


01:00:51.846 --> 01:00:54.983
Waller can trace me, you know?
She'll be sending them.


01:00:55.917 --> 01:00:58.520
What if I can make all that
go away?


01:00:59.654 --> 01:01:01.453
And what do you get out of it?


01:01:01.455 --> 01:01:05.093
Like I said a favor.
One hand washing the other.


01:01:07.361 --> 01:01:09.694
It has to do with
Professor Pyg, I...


01:01:09.696 --> 01:01:12.297
I think I finally understand
how he fits in.


01:01:12.299 --> 01:01:17.205
And for you, it would take no more effort
than freezing a tray of ice cubes.


01:01:18.939 --> 01:01:20.341
I'm listening.


01:01:24.944 --> 01:01:26.213
Don't move.


01:01:45.667 --> 01:01:47.565
Sorry.


01:01:47.567 --> 01:01:49.036
Just a cramp.


01:01:55.241 --> 01:01:57.275
<i>I'm telling you,
nothing's moving inside.</i>


01:01:57.277 --> 01:01:59.180
Not even the dust and the air.


01:02:01.314 --> 01:02:03.050
She's in there, all right.


01:02:04.218 --> 01:02:06.118
I want to set up a perimeter.


01:02:06.120 --> 01:02:08.353
Boomerang, you take
the north side.


01:02:08.355 --> 01:02:10.957
Harley. Where's Harley?


01:02:12.993 --> 01:02:15.962
We're coming to get you, Frosty!


01:02:15.964 --> 01:02:18.364
Shit.


01:02:18.366 --> 01:02:20.732
How's our leadership
thing going?


01:02:28.308 --> 01:02:30.644
You sure you got
the right address?


01:02:32.279 --> 01:02:35.813
She's in there somewhere.
Zoom may have turned her.


01:02:35.815 --> 01:02:38.719
I'll give you 30 seconds,
then I'm done with her.


01:02:40.221 --> 01:02:43.224
Look around.
Copperhead, under the house.


01:02:51.933 --> 01:02:53.265
Really?


01:02:53.267 --> 01:02:56.201
Well, she is like
Frosty the snowman.


01:02:56.203 --> 01:02:59.040
Maybe she melted.


01:03:15.189 --> 01:03:17.190
Something's off.
We're being set up.


01:03:17.192 --> 01:03:19.327
Tell Waller we found her.
Buy her some time.


01:03:20.495 --> 01:03:23.297
<i>We think we got
Frost, Waller. Standby.</i>


01:03:25.232 --> 01:03:26.701
She's done.


01:03:34.674 --> 01:03:36.410
<i>The bomb, it's down here.</i>


01:03:37.111 --> 01:03:38.313
Everybody out.


01:03:59.600 --> 01:04:02.036
I don't think he looks so good.


01:04:14.948 --> 01:04:19.486
Poor Tiger, just when I was
starting to get interested.


01:04:21.922 --> 01:04:26.292
<i>Lawton, we just got satellite
photos on those coordinates you gave me.</i>


01:04:26.294 --> 01:04:30.862
<i>This canyon shortcut will get
you to Savage ahead of Zoom.</i>


01:04:30.864 --> 01:04:33.966
<i>I'm enroute, but it might
take a while.</i>


01:04:33.968 --> 01:04:36.768
There wouldn't be a hospital
on the way, would there?


01:04:36.770 --> 01:04:38.103
Or a mortuary.


01:04:38.105 --> 01:04:40.272
<i>He's a soldier, Lawton.</i>


01:04:40.274 --> 01:04:42.475
<i>Dying's an occupational hazard.</i>


01:04:42.477 --> 01:04:47.547
<i>Keep your eyes on the road
and your head on the mission.</i>


01:04:47.549 --> 01:04:52.083
Why so glum, mate? You got
your job back, didn't ya?


01:04:52.085 --> 01:04:55.054
That bloody fool. Our true-blue.


01:04:55.056 --> 01:04:57.054
So freaking noble.


01:04:57.056 --> 01:04:59.792
Never got that we're just a puppets
trying to get through the show


01:04:59.794 --> 01:05:01.395
with our strings attached.


01:05:15.810 --> 01:05:17.810
<i>It's quite
a crib Vandal's got.</i>


01:05:17.812 --> 01:05:20.348
All that's missing is a sign
that says "Bad guy lives here."


01:05:27.721 --> 01:05:28.890
Come on.


01:05:48.776 --> 01:05:52.511
How's that?
Mighty beauty, I'd say.


01:05:52.513 --> 01:05:55.382
Let's not give each other
handjobs just yet.


01:05:59.053 --> 01:06:00.788
You see a way to get inside?


01:06:16.536 --> 01:06:18.339
I think we're being summoned.


01:06:30.951 --> 01:06:32.317
Poor Piggy.


01:06:32.319 --> 01:06:34.719
<i>Looks like he went to market.</i>


01:06:34.721 --> 01:06:37.558
This is a warning.
I'd say it's working.


01:06:55.375 --> 01:06:58.278
I presume my grieving
daughter sent you.


01:07:02.181 --> 01:07:03.714
Children.


01:07:03.716 --> 01:07:05.784
I must've sired
a hundred thousand.


01:07:05.786 --> 01:07:08.955
You think one would
show me some respect.


01:07:08.957 --> 01:07:13.428
If you wanna live another century
or two, hand over the card.


01:07:15.562 --> 01:07:18.096
That would be impossible.


01:07:18.098 --> 01:07:21.333
Mate, he's gotta have it. Doesn't
work if you don't have it on you.


01:07:21.335 --> 01:07:22.603
Not on me.


01:07:25.006 --> 01:07:26.241
In me.


01:07:27.274 --> 01:07:28.643
Professor Pyg.


01:07:33.247 --> 01:07:34.679
I don't get it.


01:07:34.681 --> 01:07:37.949
He had Pyg implant
the card in him.


01:07:37.951 --> 01:07:42.821
In such a position that to
remove it would kill me.


01:07:42.823 --> 01:07:46.692
Why do you even need it? You're
supposed to live for bloody ever.


01:07:46.694 --> 01:07:50.661
I'm immortal, not invulnerable.


01:07:50.663 --> 01:07:54.232
I've had more brushes with death
in the last ten years


01:07:54.234 --> 01:07:56.467
than all
the centuries preceding


01:07:56.469 --> 01:07:58.906
thanks to the emergence
of meta humans.


01:08:01.075 --> 01:08:02.843
I'm afraid no one lives forever.


01:08:07.614 --> 01:08:10.449
It's a neurosynaptic discharge.


01:08:10.451 --> 01:08:13.919
Blocks sensory motor
functions pretty quickly.


01:08:13.921 --> 01:08:16.890
That is, if you can
still hear me.


01:08:42.250 --> 01:08:43.718
That's a hell of an entrance.


01:08:49.756 --> 01:08:52.191
Frosty, you got the wrong side.


01:08:52.193 --> 01:08:55.259
We're the good bad guys...


01:08:55.261 --> 01:08:58.433
God, I've been wanting
to do that for a week now.


01:09:05.538 --> 01:09:07.873
Such a quick healer.


01:09:07.875 --> 01:09:10.377
You and I have that in common.


01:09:11.511 --> 01:09:13.613
Our little favor, Miss Frost?


01:09:15.349 --> 01:09:16.684
<i>Lawton.</i>


01:09:18.952 --> 01:09:22.087
We should be there at 0200 hours.
You have it yet?


01:09:22.089 --> 01:09:23.491
Getting there.


01:09:26.727 --> 01:09:28.363
Why are they freezing him?


01:09:29.129 --> 01:09:30.462
Not quite.


01:09:30.464 --> 01:09:32.431
Just bringing down
his body temperature


01:09:32.433 --> 01:09:34.435
to the point where
we can work with him.


01:09:36.336 --> 01:09:39.538
You're slow, Zoom, in the old
days, you never needed help.


01:09:39.540 --> 01:09:40.875
What's the problem?


01:09:45.746 --> 01:09:47.715
You might say everything.


01:09:54.921 --> 01:09:56.355
Nice shot.


01:09:56.357 --> 01:09:57.959
It was Batman.


01:09:59.026 --> 01:10:00.495
In another timeline.


01:10:02.229 --> 01:10:03.928
Can't say that I blame him.


01:10:03.930 --> 01:10:07.332
Thanks to me, his entire world
was going to die.


01:10:07.334 --> 01:10:12.540
Only Flash could turn back time and I was
damned if I was gonna let that happen.


01:10:13.439 --> 01:10:15.442
I never saw it coming.


01:10:18.011 --> 01:10:19.777
<i>But I felt it.</i>


01:10:19.779 --> 01:10:21.914
<i>I tried to vibrate
my inner molecules</i>


01:10:21.916 --> 01:10:25.883
<i>to save my brain even as
the bullet was tearing through.</i>


01:10:25.885 --> 01:10:30.387
<i>And in that moment, that very
infinitesimal split-second before death,</i>


01:10:30.389 --> 01:10:34.459
<i>I drew the Speed Force into me with
every ounce of will power I had left.</i>


01:10:34.461 --> 01:10:41.665
<i>And literally by time, I'd expanded my
moment of dying into day, maybe weeks.</i>


01:10:41.667 --> 01:10:44.168
But it's like operating
in a fog.


01:10:44.170 --> 01:10:47.573
Everything's a little unreal
and warped.


01:10:47.575 --> 01:10:50.174
I feel like I'm walking
through water sometimes.


01:10:50.176 --> 01:10:54.678
And then when I speed up, I can
feel my life slipping away.


01:10:54.680 --> 01:10:56.216
He's ready.


01:11:02.822 --> 01:11:05.057
I'm running on fumes now.


01:11:05.059 --> 01:11:08.496
But I've got just enough
gas left for this.


01:11:43.630 --> 01:11:45.700
Bon voyage, caveman.


01:11:57.612 --> 01:12:00.478
Shall we send Savage
some company, Banshee?


01:12:19.666 --> 01:12:24.137
You were right, speedy, nobody
knows what I'm capable of.


01:12:39.854 --> 01:12:42.323
Why, thanks. Don't mind if I do.


01:12:44.724 --> 01:12:47.793
I don't suppose you're
coming back to the fold?


01:12:47.795 --> 01:12:50.395
You supposed right, deadhead.


01:12:50.397 --> 01:12:52.030
The neck is clear.


01:12:52.032 --> 01:12:54.766
<i>And I got the card.</i>


01:12:54.768 --> 01:12:57.735
<i>Membership does have
its privileges after all.</i>


01:12:57.737 --> 01:12:59.871
Oh, really?


01:12:59.873 --> 01:13:01.438
I didn't think
you were a believer.


01:13:01.440 --> 01:13:04.209
I'm not, but a girl's
gotta make some money.


01:13:04.211 --> 01:13:06.244
How do I put
this up for auction?


01:13:06.246 --> 01:13:09.047
Let Waller know
I'll give her the first bid.


01:13:09.049 --> 01:13:12.987
You tell that trick bitch
her ass is mine, you hear?


01:13:14.621 --> 01:13:17.722
Yeah, I think she got it.


01:13:17.724 --> 01:13:19.326
<i>So long, suckers.</i>


01:13:56.663 --> 01:13:58.262
Okay.


01:13:58.264 --> 01:14:00.667
Let's see how cold-blooded
you can get.


01:14:03.237 --> 01:14:05.803
Where's the car?
How close are they doing?


01:14:05.805 --> 01:14:08.108
Coopehead's got her,
but not for long.


01:14:23.189 --> 01:14:26.760
Waller, I'll see you in hell,
you dirty...


01:14:46.679 --> 01:14:48.214
Son of a bitch.


01:14:50.117 --> 01:14:52.720
How about helping
old Digger out here, eh?


01:14:53.420 --> 01:14:55.089
Hey, hey. Whoa, hey.


01:14:59.693 --> 01:15:01.392
Two dead, Waller.


01:15:01.394 --> 01:15:04.197
<i>I'll live with it.
Just get me the card.</i>


01:15:09.469 --> 01:15:11.906
All for a magic trick.


01:15:15.776 --> 01:15:18.310
Oh, ye of little faith.


01:15:18.312 --> 01:15:20.878
She'll blow you head off,
too, you know?


01:15:20.880 --> 01:15:22.817
You're still not
getting it, love.


01:15:23.951 --> 01:15:25.116
I got the card.


01:15:25.118 --> 01:15:26.817
No onne's gonna kill me


01:15:26.819 --> 01:15:29.290
and waste a pass to the
pearly gates on this tosser.


01:15:47.608 --> 01:15:51.176
Benji! Oh, I thought
you were toast, mate.


01:15:51.178 --> 01:15:52.777
You okay?


01:15:52.779 --> 01:15:54.712
Where are the others?


01:15:54.714 --> 01:15:56.380
Oh, dead.


01:15:56.382 --> 01:15:59.551
They all killed each other
like cats in a bag.


01:15:59.553 --> 01:16:02.520
Savage, Zoom, all of them.


01:16:02.522 --> 01:16:03.989
What about the card?


01:16:03.991 --> 01:16:05.423
Well, mate, who knows?


01:16:05.425 --> 01:16:07.428
Waller's got to bring
a cleaning crew for that.


01:16:08.495 --> 01:16:09.796
Even for scum,


01:16:10.797 --> 01:16:13.231
you make a lousy liar.


01:16:13.233 --> 01:16:16.203
Watch it, kitten, you're not
the only one with claws.


01:16:26.880 --> 01:16:29.917
I know you have it.
Give it to me!


01:16:32.852 --> 01:16:34.421
Screw you.


01:16:35.822 --> 01:16:38.022
Cowboy, Zoom just took off.


01:16:38.024 --> 01:16:41.058
- Oh, yeah.
- No, you stay.


01:16:41.060 --> 01:16:42.563
Make sure they don't leave.


01:16:47.200 --> 01:16:48.903
Goddamn it.


01:17:05.352 --> 01:17:09.023
Either your reflexes are back
or mine are short.


01:17:12.625 --> 01:17:13.928
Hmm.


01:17:15.295 --> 01:17:17.464
I'd say this more than
evens things.


01:17:21.868 --> 01:17:24.835
Drop the card and walk away.


01:17:24.837 --> 01:17:27.705
What are you gonna do?
Kill me?


01:17:27.707 --> 01:17:30.141
Death by a thousand cuts, Tiger.


01:17:30.143 --> 01:17:32.112
I'll have that card
by number ten.


01:18:09.815 --> 01:18:11.385
Did I say ten?


01:18:18.090 --> 01:18:19.993
I underestimated.


01:18:35.709 --> 01:18:38.444
Do it. Save me the trouble.


01:18:39.412 --> 01:18:41.945
Maybe I'll just ward you too.


01:18:41.947 --> 01:18:47.584
I promise you, Deadshot, I'm
good for one last hit of speed.


01:18:47.586 --> 01:18:50.491
Any bullet you shoot,
I'll make sure it's lethal.


01:18:51.491 --> 01:18:52.960
So go ahead.


01:18:53.693 --> 01:18:55.428
Make my afterlife.


01:19:13.513 --> 01:19:15.515
Fuck my life.


01:19:45.511 --> 01:19:46.647
Kill me.


01:19:47.848 --> 01:19:49.847
We got him.


01:19:49.849 --> 01:19:51.718
We just crossed the finish line.


01:19:59.292 --> 01:20:00.995
I can't save you.


01:20:01.694 --> 01:20:03.096
I'm beyond


01:20:04.130 --> 01:20:05.498
salvation.


01:20:23.750 --> 01:20:26.487
You didn't want her
to have it either.


01:20:28.455 --> 01:20:30.390
She doesn't deserve it.


01:20:31.590 --> 01:20:34.460
What was her name? Your fiance?


01:20:36.462 --> 01:20:37.730
Miyoshi.


01:20:39.166 --> 01:20:40.634
Pretty name.


01:21:03.724 --> 01:21:06.460
Uh, I'll be damned.


01:21:10.596 --> 01:21:13.233
You better have that
freaking card.


01:21:20.005 --> 01:21:21.575
Not a scratch on it.


01:21:26.779 --> 01:21:29.349
Hmm, it feels cold.


01:21:30.183 --> 01:21:31.585
It's a cold world.


01:21:32.484 --> 01:21:34.718
This Zoom guy, he disappeared.


01:21:34.720 --> 01:21:38.388
I looked around...
Oh, hi, Wally, how's Trix?


01:21:38.390 --> 01:21:40.624
She would live.


01:21:42.496 --> 01:21:43.994
Are we good?


01:21:43.996 --> 01:21:47.767
No one's ever to speak
of this, Lawton, understood?


01:21:50.269 --> 01:21:52.138
I'll be seeing you, Waller.


01:21:54.107 --> 01:21:55.609
<i>Maybe in heaven.</i>

